# These patterns are matched against paths relative to the build context, so a
# bare `node_modules` only ever excluded the root one. Any workspace copy —
# apps/web/node_modules, apps/api/node_modules — was still copied in by
# `COPY apps/web ./apps/web`, landing host symlinks (absolute /Users/... paths
# on macOS) on top of the correct tree the deps stage had just installed. The
# build then failed to resolve packages that were demonstrably present.
# The `**/` forms below are what actually exclude the nested copies, so running
# `pnpm install` locally can no longer break an image build.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.env
.env.local
.env.production
**/.env.local
**/.env.production
